AI-VOX3 [V636 port]: dual-heap split -- the real fix for wlan_sta_initialize -12
=============================================================================

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
=====================

run#139's allocation tracer (patch 0013) plus the ladder probe pinned the
failure down to esp_wifi_init_internal() returning ESP_ERR_NO_MEM (257)
BEFORE a single traced allocation callback fired, with 128 KB of contiguous
internal DRAM still free -- i.e. not a plain "out of memory" story.

The root cause is proven by the v636 build of the SAME board (same openvela
manifest, same pre-compiled IDF Wi-Fi library, real hardware, WiFi/DHCP
working end-to-end):

  With BUILD_FLAT and no kernel heap, the Wi-Fi blob allocator
  (esp_malloc_internal & friends -> kmm_malloc) shares the application
  heap.  Internal DRAM pressure makes the blob's internal-only allocations
  land in PSRAM, the radio cannot DMA from PSRAM, and esp_wifi_init dies
  with ESP_ERR_NO_MEM -> wlan_sta_initialize ret=-12.

  v636 fix: CONFIG_MM_KERNEL_HEAP=y splits the heaps:
      kernel heap (kmm_malloc) = internal DRAM  <- Wi-Fi blob / DMA
      app heap    (malloc)     = PSRAM          <- LVGL / audio / app

  v636 hardware evidence:
      [V636] kernel heap (WiFi/DMA): 3fcbb460..3fceee34 size=211412
      [HEAPDBG] app heap: 3c180000..3c980000 size=8388608
      [V636] heap split: app(malloc)=PSRAM, kernel(kmm_malloc)=internal DRAM

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES
====================

CONFIG_MM_KERNEL_HEAP is NOT a Kconfig symbol in this tree (it is only
`select`ed by ESP32S3_SPIRAM_USER_HEAP, whose definition lives in the
esp-hal-3rdparty Kconfig and cannot be satisfied for BUILD_FLAT), so it can
never arrive through the defconfig -- olddefconfig would silently drop it.
It is therefore injected into .config by build.yml right after the
pre-configure step (see that file for the full rationale).

With the symbol defined, arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_allocateheap.c
takes its CONFIG_MM_KERNEL_HEAP branches:

  * up_allocate_heap()   -> MM_USER_HEAP_EXTRAM: app heap = PSRAM
  * up_allocate_kheap()  -> kernel heap = internal DRAM
                            ([_sheap+IMEM, dram0_rtos_reserved_start))
  * xtensa_add_region()  -> the COMMON_HEAP branch is disabled by
                            `!defined(MM_USER_HEAP_EXTRAM)`, so PSRAM is NOT
                            folded into the kernel heap

This patch is the minimum source change needed for that path to compile and
be observable in a FLAT build:

  1. board_memorymap.h is only generated for protected/kernel builds; the
     old `#ifdef CONFIG_MM_KERNEL_HEAP` include would break the flat build.
     Guard it on CONFIG_BUILD_PROTECTED as well.
  2. Ungalog console diagnostics (ets_printf -- syslog/nerr do NOT reach the
     console on this build) so the boot log proves the split took effect:
         [V636] app heap (malloc): ... (PSRAM)
         [V636] kernel heap (WiFi/DMA): ... (internal DRAM)

CONFIG_ESP32S3_SPIRAM_COMMON_HEAP stays y (audit gate), which is exactly
what the v636 build had; the heap layout comes out identical because
MM_USER_HEAP_EXTRAM overrides the region folding.
--- a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_allocateheap.c
+++ b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_allocateheap.c
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@
 
 #include <nuttx/config.h>
 
+#include <stdint.h>
+
 #include <debug.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 
@@ -33,10 +35,22 @@
 #include <nuttx/nuttx.h>
 #include <nuttx/userspace.h>
 #include <arch/board/board.h>
-#ifdef CONFIG_MM_KERNEL_HEAP
+/* AI-VOX3 [V636 port]: board_memorymap.h is only generated for
+ * protected/kernel builds; the FLAT kernel-heap path this board uses takes
+ * everything it needs from memory_layout.h and the ROM layout.  Guarding on
+ * CONFIG_MM_KERNEL_HEAP alone breaks the flat build (missing header).
+ */
+
+#if defined(CONFIG_MM_KERNEL_HEAP) && defined(CONFIG_BUILD_PROTECTED)
 #include <arch/board/board_memorymap.h>
 #endif
 
+/* AI-VOX3 [V636 port]: ungalog console output so the heap split is visible
+ * in the boot log (syslog/nerr does not reach the console on this build).
+ */
+
+extern int ets_printf(const char *fmt, ...);
+
 #include <arch/esp32s3/memory_layout.h>
 #include "xtensa.h"
 #include "hardware/esp32s3_rom_layout.h"
@@ -120,6 +134,16 @@
 
   usize = utop - ubase;
 
+  /* AI-VOX3 [V636 port]: make the heap split visible at boot. */
+
+#ifdef MM_USER_HEAP_EXTRAM
+  ets_printf("[V636] app heap (malloc): 0x%08x..0x%08x size=%u (PSRAM)\n",
+             (unsigned)ubase, (unsigned)utop, (unsigned)usize);
+#else
+  ets_printf("[V636] app heap (malloc): 0x%08x..0x%08x size=%u (internal DRAM, SHARED with radio)\n",
+             (unsigned)ubase, (unsigned)utop, (unsigned)usize);
+#endif
+
   minfo("Heap: start=%" PRIxPTR " end=%" PRIxPTR " size=%zu\n",
         ubase, utop, usize);
 
@@ -177,6 +201,14 @@
 
   ksize = ktop - kbase;
 
+  /* AI-VOX3 [V636 port]: this is the DMA-capable heap the Wi-Fi blob's
+   * os_adapter allocators (esp_malloc_internal & friends -> kmm_malloc)
+   * draw from.  Nothing else competes with the radio for it.
+   */
+
+  ets_printf("[V636] kernel heap (WiFi/DMA): 0x%08x..0x%08x size=%u (internal DRAM)\n",
+             (unsigned)kbase, (unsigned)ktop, (unsigned)ksize);
+
   minfo("Heap: start=%" PRIxPTR " end=%" PRIxPTR " size=%zu\n",
         kbase, ktop, ksize);
 
